{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UNUNK8C8rDoRAc92ymyEzk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty, running as a persistent local web app on this machine (`PUTER`/`gwl-server`). Grounded claims:\n\n- **Purpose â€” a single-folder personal productivity system.** Everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no OneDrive, no syncing). It manages tasks, projects, an inbox, and per-domain work (academic, commercial, family, writing) as plain-markdown files that are the source of truth â€” no database, no binary formats.\n\n- **What it does â€” task lifecycle over markdown.** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, each editable with priority/energy/domain/due/notes. Changes are made through a browser dashboard or CLI and written straight back to the markdown files, with daily activity logs.\n\n- **How it ships/runs â€” a stdlib-only Python web server.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary interface: a self-contained HTTP server (Python stdlib only, one declared exception) that regenerates the full dashboard HTML per request and binds `http://localhost:8777`. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`; `anchor.py` is the CLI mirror that also emits static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has grown an R&D \"cockpit\" surface (v2â†’v4).** Each project gets a window that runs the **trio** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) as durable, isolated, server-side terminal sessions. v4 \"Project Cockpit\" gives each lane (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) a tile with a single honest status light, inline expanding panels with cached summaries + a resizable terminal, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), and per-project cost/tokens/time rollups.\n\n- **The terminal substrate is real ConPTY with git-worktree isolation.** v3/v4 run interactive sessions over a Windows ConPTY PTY (the lone permitted native dep, `pywinpty`, lazily imported in `pty_manager.py` only), each in its own git worktree/branch, streamed to xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket (`term_ws`) with an SSE fallback. A skill auto-loads and greets exactly once per session.\n\n- **Quality is enforced by a daily health check.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file and exercising every endpoint plus the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (never touching the live `:8777` service or real data); failures surface as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **The single declared deliverable is `anchor_gui.py`** â€” the running app itself, which is pinnable and runnable as an ephemeral preview on an OS-assigned port hard-guarded to never be 8777.\n\nThe current branch (`master`) has uncommitted changes and new `.anchor/` runtime state, consistent with the v4 build having recently merged (commit `38fd70e`) and been deployed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f0ea2ff2-d840-4c5f-959e-dad1a2b51620","uuid":"4a9c2e73-18c0-4b95-af27-66a3c6338df5","request_id":"req_011Cc1fTR8vouWK1GeKwisnp"}
